RenHDrum 0.4.0, the upstream release binary
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/tree/v0.4.0
https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum/releases/tag/v0.4.0

Since 0.4.0 the upstream build links the C runtime statically (.cargo/config.toml sets
-C target-feature=+crt-static for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc), so the release binary is
shipped here as it is: no rebuild is needed for players without the Visual C++
redistributable. renhdrum.dll is the release asset byte for byte (438272 bytes), and its
sha256 matches the one on the release page. Its dependencies:

    api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0.dll
    KERNEL32.dll
    ntdll.dll

No VCRUNTIME140.dll, no MSVCP140.dll, no api-ms-win-crt-*.dll. It exports 50 names (the
47 of 0.3.0 plus renhdrum_settings_resolve_pure and the two renhdrum_valve_grip_* calls);
renhdrum_version() returns 0x000400.

renhdrum.h is include/renhdrum.h from the v0.4.0 tag, byte for byte. The release asset
of the same name differs only in its CRLF line endings
(sha256 930528372d9e37c4b8c566a864aff4f696e6a00ca074bee6b7a4b7f89140a506).

853ddc07fcf2c1011f7dcae791c61d405aca378b5fd46248006e0e5880153a59  renhdrum.dll
32d8da0d06b34704d3d89873d53c1b4d030acfbe820bd629e8c25d18b9b93a0a  renhdrum.h

LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and NOTICE are copied from the same tag: the core of
RenHDrum is dual licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0, and NOTICE asks for
"Copyright (c) 2026 Three-Dola" to be kept. The GPL-3.0-or-later parts of that
project (integrations/brontide, integrations/recomp-c/reference) are not used
here: the host calls the prebuilt library through its C ABI and does not build
any of its sources.
